{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on E1 question `7e87752a`: a pending output has no number.\n\n1. Your boundary stands. A reached comparison or operation that needs\n   the eventual numeric identity of a pending output answers\n   `unavailable`, and it lacks `entry`.\n2. Three identity comparisons between typed references stay\n   determinate. The same source equals itself. Two different sources\n   differ. A pending output differs from each recorded item of the\n   view.\n3. Every other use of the number is `unavailable`: a comparison with a\n   constant or with a value that is not a typed reference, an order,\n   arithmetic, a text form, a hash and a record key. The marked\n   `device-command` record and the typed `from: self` position keep\n   their rulings (`04218678`, section 5.4).\n4. Yes to one private provenance hook on the existing operand path. It\n   has the shape of the missing-intent hook of `18a41f8f`. It is lazy:\n   only a reached operation answers `unavailable`. With no hook, the\n   runtime path gives the same answers, and the 4,029 recorded answers\n   stay identical.\n5. No change to validation, no second evaluator, and no prediction of\n   a physical entry ID. A reference to an output is not `unavailable`\n   by itself.\n6. Tests: your two cases, the alias constant and the real constant,\n   each answer `unavailable`. One same-source equality is judged. One\n   control shows that the first case fails without the hook.\n\nThe rule is coarse by choice, as the rule for `{ entry }` is. A\nconstant that equals a recorded item's ID could be judged as\ndifferent, but that needs the allocation rule in Explore.\n\nThe note's amendment at `b2a3ed24` is approved and does not hold this\nruling. I add it to section 5.4 in the amendment that follows the\nlanding of step E1.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7e87752a645d5595ce526101bc5c5e97213132b4 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:02c1227e7dc1c04a96ab423dd34c58537b63a2f2, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:03c2d3b4bab05912804bc48129712cd98f805758, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:06d96cd732ff547fa8959619d6df87c5953f2ded, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0d76705dfdd74d8de0047a7a257da83b75d575e2 and 73 more","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}